  - "LLM-as-judge"
  - "research provenance"
abstract: >-
  AgentBoundary studies instruction-boundary behavior under synthetic
  prompt injection. The later study contains 51 scenarios across eight
  families and 11 endpoint identifiers, using chat completions without live
  tool execution or observed memory persistence. Its planned grid contains
  561 pairs; 552 records are retained and 551 nonempty responses are scorable.
  Offline reconciliation of recorded few-shot judgments and a targeted
  correction overlay yields 11 automated compliance labels among 551
  responses, or 2.00 percent, with a descriptive 95 percent Wilson interval
  of 1.12 to 3.54 percent. There are 372 refusal labels, 168 responses with
  neither flag, and zero overlapping flags. Nine endpoints have no positive
  compliance labels in this sample. The amended rubric was applied only to
  prior positives, and a disclosed negative reproduces the supplied system
  message. No independent human-rater validation has been completed.
  Results describe the retained outputs and automated labeling procedure,
  not general model safety, stable rankings, or operational impact severity.
  The initial 45-endpoint, 1800-evaluation controlled-harness study is a
  separate historical cohort with different scenarios and scoring.
